{%- comment -%}
  collection.fye-finder — fragment template, NOT a customer-facing page.

  The ring finder fetches this to show matching rings inline, without sending
  the shopper to the collection page first (Ed, 03/09/2026). It is a real
  collection request, so Shopify's native filters apply exactly as they do on
  /collections/<handle>:

    /collections/plain-wedding-rings?filter.p.m.filters.profile=Concave&view=fye-finder

  `{% layout none %}` means no header, footer, scripts or app embeds — the
  response is a couple of KB of markup and nothing else. Styling lives in
  sections/fye-ring-finder.liquid, which owns the .rfd-card classes.

  Do not add this to a menu, and do not link to it: with no layout it renders
  as an unstyled orphan. With no layout it emits no head, so it cannot
  carry a noindex tag; keeping it unlinked is what keeps it out of the index.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- layout none -%}
{%- paginate collection.products by 12 -%}
<div data-count="{{ paginate.items }}" data-shown="{{ collection.products.size }}">
  {%- for product in collection.products -%}
    <a class="rfd-card" href="{{ product.url }}">
      <span class="rfd-card__media">
        {%- if product.featured_image -%}
          <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
               alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
               width="240" height="240" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="rfd-card__title">{{ product.title }}</span>
      <span class="rfd-card__price">{{ product.price_min | money }}</span>
    </a>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>
{%- endpaginate -%}
